    "result": "I fixed the regression in `_split_kwds` in `sqlparse/filters/reindent.py`. I couldn't run the test suite, so the fix is untested.\n\nThe check for inserting a line break before keywords like `FROM` was inverted. It added a newline only when the preceding token already ended in one, and skipped it otherwise. That is why `select *from bar;` never got its line break. I added the missing `not`.\n\nThe one-line change matches how I remember the upstream code, but I didn't compare against it.\n\nBoth times I tried to run pytest, the shell refused — the first call for chaining commands, the second for the `python` path. A plain `pytest tests -q` from the workspace root will confirm the 26 checks pass again."
  },
